{"repositoryId":1193370254,"availability":"available","full":"sudosilo/mission-operator","name":"mission-operator","description":"Location aware scanner console for nearby aircraft, radios, mesh nodes, and towers.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-03-27T06:33:25Z","updated":"2026-10-16T01:57:24Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mission-operator.vercel.app","topics":["aviation","radio","react","tool","vercel"],"demo":"https://mission-operator.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.672Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.672Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.672Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.672Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Mission Operator is a field scanner console for anyone curious about what is in the air and on the airwaves nearby.","It asks for the device location, then scans and lists nearby signals by type. Aircraft come from live flight data. Other types include cell towers, Wi-Fi access points, Bluetooth, ham repeaters, Meshtastic and Helium nodes, and rail. A logbook keeps what was found, and a settings panel adjusts the scan.","Checked every morning by Control Troll, an automated test system that loads every app and clicks through its features."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sudosilo/mission-operator/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d77204bcf4067a4fd5e422c5ceeb398a59163fc2eb4e40a6cc67eb2eee5f9154","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.758Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.758Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Mission Operator is a field scanner console for anyone curious about what is in the air and on the airwaves nearby.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sudosilo/mission-operator/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"d77204bcf4067a4fd5e422c5ceeb398a59163fc2eb4e40a6cc67eb2eee5f9154","sou